### HireLens API — ready-made requests
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or copy as curl).
### Start the server first: pnpm --filter @hirelens/api dev

@host = http://localhost:4000
# 1) Sign up (email/password), then copy the better-auth.session_token
#    cookie from the response headers into @cookie below.
@cookie = better-auth.session_token=PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### Health (public)
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Sign up — response sets the session cookie
POST {{host}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
content-type: application/json

{
  "name": "Recruiter One",
  "email": "recruiter@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ng-Passw0rd!123"
}

### Sign in (after the first sign-up)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
content-type: application/json

{
  "email": "recruiter@example.com",
  "password": "Str0ng-Passw0rd!123"
}

### Create organization (auth required)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/organization/create
content-type: application/json
cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "name": "Acme Recruiting",
  "slug": "acme-recruiting"
}

### List jobs
GET {{host}}/api/jobs
cookie: {{cookie}}

### Create a job
POST {{host}}/api/jobs
content-type: application/json
cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "title": "Senior Backend Engineer",
  "description": "Own our payments platform. Deep TypeScript, Postgres, and distributed-systems experience required.",
  "status": "open"
}

### Import a rubric (validate + store as next version)
POST {{host}}/api/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/rubrics
content-type: application/json
cookie: {{cookie}}

{
  "rubric": {
    "version": 1,
    "key": "backend-eng",
    "title": "Backend Engineer",
    "criteria": [
      {
        "key": "system-design",
        "title": "System Design",
        "weight": 2,
        "scale": [
          { "label": "0", "description": "none" },
          { "label": "1", "description": "minimal" },
          { "label": "2", "description": "basic" },
          { "label": "3", "description": "solid" },
          { "label": "4", "description": "strong" },
          { "label": "5", "description": "expert" }
        ],
        "doNotUse": []
      },
      {
        "key": "databases",
        "title": "Databases",
        "weight": 1,
        "scale": [
          { "label": "0", "description": "none" },
          { "label": "1", "description": "minimal" },
          { "label": "2", "description": "basic" },
          { "label": "3", "description": "solid" },
          { "label": "4", "description": "strong" },
          { "label": "5", "description": "expert" }
        ],
        "doNotUse": []
      },
      {
        "key": "testing",
        "title": "Testing",
        "weight": 1,
        "scale": [
          { "label": "0", "description": "none" },
          { "label": "1", "description": "minimal" },
          { "label": "2", "description": "basic" },
          { "label": "3", "description": "solid" },
          { "label": "4", "description": "strong" },
          { "label": "5", "description": "expert" }
        ],
        "doNotUse": []
      },
      {
        "key": "communication",
        "title": "Communication",
        "weight": 1,
        "scale": [
          { "label": "0", "description": "none" },
          { "label": "1", "description": "minimal" },
          { "label": "2", "description": "basic" },
          { "label": "3", "description": "solid" },
          { "label": "4", "description": "strong" },
          { "label": "5", "description": "expert" }
        ],
        "doNotUse": []
      }
    ],
    "exclusions": []
  }
}

### Derive a rubric from the job description with the LLM (needs HIRELENS_LLM_*)
POST {{host}}/api/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/rubrics/derive
cookie: {{cookie}}

### Upload one resume (PDF/DOCX/TXT/MD)
POST {{host}}/api/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/candidates
content-type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary
cookie: {{cookie}}

--Boundary
content-disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="resume.txt"
content-type: text/plain

JORDAN AVERY
Senior Backend Engineer - jordan@example.com
EXPERIENCE
Senior Backend Engineer - Acme Corp - 2021 - Present
- Led migration to Kubernetes.
--Boundary--

### Upload a ZIP of resumes
POST {{host}}/api/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/candidates/zip
content-type: multipart/form-data; boundary=Boundary
cookie: {{cookie}}

--Boundary
content-disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="batch.zip"
content-type: application/zip

< ./batch.zip
--Boundary--

### Score all candidates against the latest rubric (needs HIRELENS_LLM_*)
POST {{host}}/api/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/score
cookie: {{cookie}}

### Scoring run history
GET {{host}}/api/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/runs
cookie: {{cookie}}
